+For the same exact controlled target, the synthetic uncontrolled and
+controlled state RMS values are $3.58130\times10^{-2}$ and $3.39772\times10^{-5}$,
+respectively. The peak synthetic generalized-force norm is $6.07119\times10^{-2}$,
+and direct substitution of the control into the original mechanical
+field differs from the stated closed field by at most $1.241\times10^{-16}$.
+These dimensionless values have no magnetic-hardware interpretation.
+
+
+The old v10 display-precision coefficients in material B are retained
+only as historical input. No old frequency, modal map, control peak or
+energy threshold enters these new-baseline tables. These added tests
+provide neither full-network fitting, higher-mode closed-loop trajectories,
+COMSOL or hardware validation, nor a finite-amplitude KAM certificate.
